{
    "background_story": "In the scorching deserts of the American Southwest, a legendary snake named Osiris roamed the dunes. He was a coachwhip, known for his striking appearance and agility. Osiris was a master of stealth, able to slither through the sand with ease, striking with lightning speed when prey crossed his path. But Osiris was no ordinary coachwhip - he possessed a unique gift. He could sense the emotions of those around him, and would often appear to travelers lost in the desert, guiding them to safety with his hypnotic gaze. The locals revered Osiris as a mystical creature, a symbol of protection and guidance. His reputation grew, and people would venture into the desert, hoping to catch a glimpse of the elusive coachwhip, Osiris, the desert's guardian spirit.",
